{
  "headline": "Zuckerberg says Meta's Muse has passed 10 million users and about 25% of people who set it up use it daily",
  "sources": [
    { "name": "TechCrunch", "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/21/meta-says-muse-has-over-10m-users-with-shopping-a-top-activity/" }
  ],
  "bullets": [
    "TechCrunch reports Meta said on its Q3 earnings call that Muse \"has been adopted by more than 10 million users, confirming estimates released earlier this week by market intelligence firm Sensor Tower,\" and that Zuckerberg \"said about 25% of people who set up Muse now use it daily.\"",
    "On commerce, TechCrunch reports \"over a quarter of Muse's engaged users who were shopping via the AI agent had an average purchase size of over $200,\" and that Meta plans to keep Muse free for most users and \"keep a percentage of the commerce taking place on the platform.\"",
    "Zuckerberg put a number on the compute problem, quoted by TechCrunch: \"On the compute side, we are building out the capacity to serve more than a billion people over the next few years. In the near term, Muse is very compute-intensive to run, but we expect to improve its cost efficiency by more than 10x in the next year, which will enable it to be profitable once the revenue lines are at scale.\"",
    "Every figure is Meta's own, stated on an earnings call, and TechCrunch is the only outlet reporting them. The 10x cost-efficiency improvement is a forecast, not a result, and Meta has not published Muse revenue. Note that TechCrunch's framing of Reality Labs losses differs from Meta's filing, which guides 2026 losses to $18-19 billion."
  ],
  "topics": ["meta", "agents", "earnings"],
  "impact": "neutral",
  "flags": ["company-claim", "single-source"]
},
